---
import "../styles/global.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const href = (path: string) => `${base}${path}` || "/";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <meta
      http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
      content="default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; connect-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self'"
    />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Nindova is a quiet fifteen-minute ritual that puts the day away, crosses one Vista, and ends itself."
    />
    <link rel="icon" href={href("/favicon.svg")} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <title>Nindova — put the day away</title>
  </head>
  <body class="landing">
    <header class="nav-edge" aria-label="Primary navigation">
      <a class="wordmark" href={href("/")} aria-label="Nindova home">Nindova</a>
      <a class="nav-action" href={href("/play/")}>Play tonight</a>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="window-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="hero-premise">A Punjabi night room after a long day.</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Put the day away.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">
            A quiet fifteen-minute ritual: clear one desk, cross one changing Vista, follow the last
            light home, and leave. The Session ends itself.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="action-primary" href={href("/play/")}>Enter Nindova</a>
            <a class="action-text" href={href("/docs/")}>Read the contract <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <p class="trust-line">Nothing to win. Nothing tracked. Nothing you can do wrong.</p>
        </div>

        <figure class="window-art">
          <div class="phulkari-frame">
            <img
              src={href("/media/session-punjabi-portrait.png")}
              width="375"
              height="812"
              alt="The real Nindova Session: an indigo rain window, phulkari border, lamp-lit desk, letter, and mustard-field Vista controls."
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>Rendered Session · Punjabi night room</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="material-world" aria-labelledby="world-title">
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">The visual world</p>
          <h2 id="world-title">Indigo night. Marigold thread. Earth after rain.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Nindova draws from Punjabi material craft and Indian landscapes: phulkari geometry, carved
          jali rhythm, brass, terracotta, mustard fields, and a quiet riverside harbor. The references
          stay specific and everyday—never religious decoration or generic “exotic” styling.
        </p>
        <div class="material-key" aria-label="Visual materials">
          <span>Phulkari</span><span>Indigo</span><span>Terracotta</span><span>Brass</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="arc" aria-labelledby="arc-title">
        <header class="section-head">
          <h2 id="arc-title">One fixed arc. No menu.</h2>
          <p>The room changes. The promise does not.</p>
        </header>
        <ol class="arc-steps">
          <li>
            <span class="arc-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <h3>Put away</h3>
            <p>Name a thought if you want. Move each visible thing off the desk. Help increases as effort fades.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="arc-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <h3>Cross</h3>
            <p>The window opens to meadow or harbor. One small procession moves toward shelter.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="arc-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <h3>Leave</h3>
            <p>Follow the last light back. Turn the sign. The room goes dark, and the Session is over.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="two-loops" aria-labelledby="loops-title">
        <div class="loop-copy">
          <h2 id="loops-title">Satisfying now.<br />Inviting later.</h2>
          <p>
            Nindova can feel good while it is happening. It must never use that feeling to make this
            Session harder to leave.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="loop-rules">
          <p><strong>Inside tonight</strong><span>Touch, settle, cross, close.</span></p>
          <p><strong>Between nights</strong><span>A changed window. A quiet trace. Nothing owed.</span></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="dawn" aria-labelledby="dawn-title">
        <figure class="dawn-art">
          <img
            src={href("/media/dawn-punjabi.png")}
            width="712"
            height="446"
            alt="Nindova Dawn rendered over a Punjabi mustard meadow, with a rabbit beside a wooden fence and a phulkari border."
          />
          <figcaption>Rendered Dawn · first light in the mustard meadow</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="dawn-copy">
          <h2 id="dawn-title">Morning keeps one still.</h2>
          <p>
            After a completed Session, Dawn can return the Vista at first light as a local still and
            a subtle silent loop. No notification brings you back. You choose whether to look.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="local" aria-labelledby="local-title">
        <p class="local-statement" id="local-title">Your night stays on this device.</p>
        <div class="local-detail">
          <p>No account.</p>
          <p>No analytics.</p>
          <p>No sleep score.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
        <h2 id="closing-title">Fifteen minutes. Then dark.</h2>
        <p>
          Nindova is behavioral design, not a sleep tracker or treatment. It is intended for ages 13
          and up. Persistent sleep difficulty deserves evidence-based care such as CBT-I with a
          qualified clinician.
        </p>
        <a class="action-primary" href={href("/play/")}>Play tonight</a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="foot-stmt">
      <p class="foot-stmt-line">The room goes dark.<br />Nindova stops.</p>
      <div class="foot-meta">
        <a class="wordmark" href={href("/")}>Nindova</a>
        <nav aria-label="Footer navigation">
          <a href={href("/docs/")}>Docs</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/udhawan97/Nindova">GitHub</a>
        </nav>
        <span>Behavioral design study · 13+</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
